# Packages/Sentinel v1.0.0 — boundary guard, live
# Date: 2026-09-03T08:08:46Z
#
# Proves the guard that lets this package be published: Sentinel refuses
# to read baselines from inside the Toolbelt checkout.

$ python3 -m sentinel --baselines <repo>/Packages/Sentinel/baselines hosts
sentinel: baselines directory <repo>/Packages/Sentinel/baselines is inside the Toolbelt repo at <repo>. Baselines name hosts, addresses and kernel versions and this repo may be published; keep them outside it (default: ~/.claude/data/baselines).
exit=2

$ python3 -m sentinel --baselines <repo> hosts
sentinel: baselines directory <repo> is inside the Toolbelt repo at <repo>. Baselines name hosts, addresses and kernel versions and this repo may be published; keep them outside it (default: ~/.claude/data/baselines).
exit=2

$ python3 -m sentinel --baselines /nonexistent hosts
sentinel: baselines directory /nonexistent does not exist. Sentinel ships the method, not the data — create it and add hosts.json (see examples/hosts.example.json).
exit=2
